A="""[excited] Your side hustle made two hundred dollars this month. Nice! [short pause] [curious] Now do the math nobody posts online. Divide it by the hours you actually put in. Twenty hours? [pause] That's ten dollars an hour. [sighs] No boss… but also no sick days, no guaranteed pay, and nobody to complain to. [cautiously] And two hundred a month is what the TYPICAL side hustler made, in Bankrate's 2025 survey. The average was eight hundred and eighty-five… because a few people make a LOT. [mischievously] So before you celebrate, check your hourly rate. Because"""
B="""[curious] One hundred and sixty-eight hours a week. That's all you get. [short pause] Take off sleep: fifty-six. Your job: forty. Commuting, eating, showering, just existing: about forty more. [pause] What's left? Around thirty hours. That's your side hustle's ENTIRE budget. [dramatically] And here's the cruel part. When your side hustle works, it wants MORE of them. More orders. More messages. [sighs] More evenings gone. This is the time wall, and it's where a huge number of side hustles quietly die. [warmly] The ones that survive raise their prices, drop their worst customers, and automate the boring stuff. Because the problem was never the idea. It was the hours. [mischievously] And no matter how good your idea is…"""
